From 3eb334ce2138fc594981b9c403700b05d7e058a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:47:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 070/211] clk: sunxi-ng: add support for the A733 CPU clock
 controller

The CPU clocks of the A733 sit in a block of their own. The cluster and
DSU PLLs are of a "linear" kind not seen in the CCUs so far: they run
straight off the oscillator with an 8-bit multiplier, the only divider
lives in the consumer's clock register, and new factors have to be
latched with an update bit before the PLL relocks. Model them with a
small set of clock ops here rather than stretching one of the generic
PLL types.

The backup PLL is a regular one and is left to the NKMP code. Each
consumer is a mux, which has to run from something else while its PLL
relocks. The manual offers three backup sources per cluster: the 26 MHz
oscillator, the backup PLL and a periphery PLL output. Pick the
periphery PLL, 1.2 GHz for the cores and 600 MHz for the DSU. The
oscillator would leave the whole cluster at 26 MHz for the duration of
the relock, which is slow enough that an interrupt arriving in that
window can keep its softirq looping for good, so the mux is never
switched back and the cluster stays there.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig               |  10 +
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile              |   2 +
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c | 350 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 362 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig
